            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="0922" n="786" xml:id="pg786"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3342 supp.: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-01T20:00:00-04:00">May 1, 1929—8
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>46. Your 63, April 17, 8 p.m., paragraph (<hi rendition="#italic">h</hi>). The
                    following telegrams which were sent to the Ambassador in Peru are quoted for
                    your information.</p>
                <p>[Here follow the texts of telegrams Nos. 48, April 26, 7 p.m., and 49, April 27,
                    1 p.m., printed on <ref target="#pg779">pages 779</ref> and <ref target="#pg780"
                        >780</ref>.]</p>
                <p>The Ambassador in Peru in his telegram No. 87, April 30, 3 p.m., stated, among
                    other things, the following:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of paragraph two of telegram No. 87, printed on <ref
                        target="#pg783">page 783</ref>.]</p>
                <p>Today the Department replied as follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the text of telegram No. 51, May 1, 4 p.m., to the Ambassador in
                    Peru, printed on <ref target="#pg785">page 785</ref>.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
